{"text": "Timeline of First Union major bank merger partners\nSelections only, not a complete list\n\n1908\n\n1958\n\n1962\n\n1963\n\n1964\n\n1967\n\n1968\n\n1975\n\n1981\n\n1983\n\n1985\n\n1986\n\nUnion National Bank founded in Charlotte, NC\n\nUnion National Bank merges with First National Bank and Trust Company of Asheville,\nforming First Union National Bank of North Carolina\nBank of Lenoir and Union National Bank of Lenoir\n\nThe Jackson County Bank of Sylva, extending services to the far western section of NC\nCity National Bank of Winston-Salem\n\nMergers with Commercial Bank of Lexington, Bank of Greensboro, The Scottish Bank of\nLumberton are completed.\n\nCameron-Brown, the nation\u2019s 15\" largest mortgage banking firm, merges with First\nUnion\n\nAcquires Citizens Bank and Trust of Southern Pines and Bank of Wendell\n\nHolding company First Union National Bancorp, Inc. is established.\n\nHolding Company renamed First Union Corporation\n\nAcquires First National Bank of Catawba County and First National Bank of Albermarle.\n\nAcquired Piedmont Corporation, bank holding company with assets of $133 million,\nheadquartered in Charlotte.\n\nEnters Florida with acquisition of Atlantic Bancorporation of Jacksonville, FL and Dade-\ncity based Central Florida Bank Corporation\nMerger with Northwestern Financial Corporation, North Carolina\u2019s 4\" largest banking\norganization, was announced.\n\nExpansion into South Carolina with acquisition of Southern Bancorporation, South\nCarolina\u2019s 4\" largest banking company.\n\nFirst Union/Page 1 of 2",
